  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Headphones** (1 review, 1 other source): Robin Eubanks sat in on trombone for this song; Track 4 is singled out as a showcase of the band's power [1][2]\n- **JCA** (1 other source): JCA runs straight into Stay, per the uploader's setlist notation [1]\n- **Stay** (1 other source): Robin Eubanks also played trombone here; the song follows JCA without a break [1]\n- **Kraz Fast** (1 review): Track 8 is also named as proof of the band's strength [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **J-Live**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Headphones**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **JCA**: rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- **Kraz Fast**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Crosstown Traffic [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2004-07-15.sr69.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 14 songs; 124 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Robin Eubanks made a guest appearance during the show [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2004-07-15.sr69.flac16**: taped by Rhys Herrmann; transferred by Rhys Herrmann; source: Earthworks SR69's > Edirol UA-5 (w-mod) > Toshiba Portege 3480 > Soundforge 5.0 (24/48) [1]",
